  "Number": 3,
  "Question": "What is the largest difference that can be formed by subtracting two numbers chosen from the set \\(\\{-16, -4, 0, 2, 4, 12\\}?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(10\\)",
    "B": "\\(12\\)",
    "C": "\\(16\\)",
    "D": "\\(28\\)",
    "E": "\\(48\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "A difference increases when the first number increases or the number being subtracted decreases. Therefore the largest difference comes from subtracting the least number in the set, \\(-16\\), from the greatest, \\(12\\):\n\\[\n12-(-16)=12+16=28.\n\\]\nBoth numbers are available, so this largest value is attained. The answer is \\(\\boxed{28}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
